  "body": "Found by mkinney's QA runs (p02, p03, p04, p05, p08) and reproduced on a minimal part by a separate verification run on 2026-11-18, CamCraft main `83867fd7` (= v0.24.0 code). Minimal repro projects and posted programs are kept on mkinney's machines and can be attached.\n\nWhat happens: a 2D Chamfer with no picked edges (auto edge detection) on a part with a 1 mm chamfer on its outer top edge and a sharp-edged pocket (model X20-40, Y15-25) chamfers the outer edge correctly AND the pocket's top edge, which is sharp in the CAD:\n```\nG0 X22 Y17.003 Z25\nG1 X22 Y17.003 Z-1.8 F300\nG1 X22 Y17 Z-1.8 F1200\nG1 X41.995 Y17 Z-1.8 F1200\n```\n`verify` returns ok with **gouge 0**, and the program posts. At chamfer width 2.5 the cut goes 2.5 mm into the model, still gouge 0. No note says which edges the op picked.\n\nWhy P1: a cut into the finished part posts with a clean verify (Prime Directive: never gouge, never pass it silently).\n\nRepro: plate with a pocket; Tormach 770MX; fit stock; Face to the part top; `chamfer2_d` with CM-0600-90, `width 0.8`, no picks; generate, verify, post, render_stock.\n\nDone means: auto detection takes only edges the model chamfers (or refuses / lists the picked edges for the user to confirm), and the stock sim flags any chamfer pass that removes model material; pinned by a test with this plate (sharp pocket edge untouched, or a gouge reported).\n",
